# Optional reverse proxy for harness servers. NOT required to run the
# harnesses — each server already serves both /api/* and the built client SPA
# on its own PORT (see each server .env). Use this only if/when you want a
# stable port-80 LAN hostname instead of remembering ports, or to front multiple
# harnesses behind one Caddy instance later.
#
# Intentionally LAN-only, unlike track-web's Caddyfile: no public DNS record,
# no automatic Let's Encrypt. This harness family is meant to run somewhere with
# no exposure to the public internet (e.g. a NUC on the home LAN) — see
# docs/arch/pi-harness.md's security notes on why (the bash/write/edit tool
# surface is a much bigger blast radius than anything track-web exposes
# publicly). Replace the hostnames with names you've pointed at this box
# (router DNS, /etc/hosts, mDNS/avahi) or just proxy by IP.
#
# Formatting: tabs not spaces. Run `caddy fmt --overwrite Caddyfile` after edits.

deck.local {
	reverse_proxy localhost:4100
}

introspect.local {
	reverse_proxy localhost:4200
}
